                        ],
                        "form": "feezed"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "38343a61-a200-4254-9b6b-66dcd10be473",
                        "entry_id": "d60d249c-7539-3008-a8be-42bb59c6d6aa",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "feezed"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a52d71c1-4936-346d-b16a-58ddefd1c32c",
                        "entry_id": "d60d249c-7539-3008-a8be-42bb59c6d6aa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To twist or turn with a screw-like motion; to screw."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Scotland",
                            "also",
                            "dialectal",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3bff819e-56fa-492b-904c-d8fe0628ff8d",
                                "sense_id": "a52d71c1-4936-346d-b16a-58ddefd1c32c",
                                "text": "What pushing and crushing\nAmang the lads and lasses;\nWhat squeezing and feezing\nWi' ilka ane that passes"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5f69d47b-3a63-4eab-93b9-aeeac8a29c7d",
                                "sense_id": "a52d71c1-4936-346d-b16a-58ddefd1c32c",
                                "text": "For forty years—like Rob the Ranter, I've feezed about my rhymin' chanter' Blawn up the bag, and cock'd my bonnet, And tried to \"croon an ault Scots sonnet,\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b343e4dd-31e7-415e-a980-bf193c00ef71",
                                "sense_id": "a52d71c1-4936-346d-b16a-58ddefd1c32c",
                                "text": "The superintendent stated that he had tried it, or examined it, the day before and could not budge or feeze it."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c0193e76-397f-39b5-87ac-b248ffbf5194",
                        "entry_id": "d60d249c-7539-3008-a8be-42bb59c6d6aa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To insinuate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Scotland",
                            "broadly",
                            "dialectal",
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "aa37a9fd-559b-3369-856c-9ab21fe69c4d",
                        "entry_id": "d60d249c-7539-3008-a8be-42bb59c6d6aa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To untwist; to unravel, as the end of a thread or rope."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Scotland",
                            "dialectal",
                            "intransitive",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "da6b6114-78a9-46bb-bcaa-77b5f3aab059",
                                "sense_id": "aa37a9fd-559b-3369-856c-9ab21fe69c4d",
                                "text": "In short, Tibbie made maist praiseworthy efforts to feeze her fingers oot o' my loof as lang as I held them fast."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc13f418-eecb-4568-adb6-365849f3012d",
                                "sense_id": "aa37a9fd-559b-3369-856c-9ab21fe69c4d",
                                "text": "The thread that joins us baith will sune Feeze oot and snap in twa!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4bbe6868-92f2-4022-a1c3-0c51972caec4",
                                "sense_id": "aa37a9fd-559b-3369-856c-9ab21fe69c4d",
                                "text": "I can't feeze it out among these strange entanglements of circumstance and personalities."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "50b46700-2d8a-3b19-a8c2-0c604a1d29b8",
                        "entry_id": "d60d249c-7539-3008-a8be-42bb59c6d6aa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To rub hard; to do a piece of work with passion."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Scotland",
                            "dialectal",
                            "figuratively",
                            "obsolete",
