                                "sense_id": "238844c1-f53c-39b5-82ac-515b261bf2ac",
                                "text": "“How does the snow come;\" he asks. “Mama says God makes it snow. Does he keep it up there, and all the rain, too. I s'd t'ink he'd feeze. Mama al'as says, come in Willie, you'll feeze in 'e snow.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2fb21cf8-826b-4f54-a7f2-11b2d2304e43",
                                "sense_id": "238844c1-f53c-39b5-82ac-515b261bf2ac",
                                "text": "“Fine weather for feezing! fine weather for feezing! answered the latter, with a mocking look which Sylvandire caught, and which frightened her."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f23bed51-1370-43c7-83e6-9520d6383946",
                                "sense_id": "238844c1-f53c-39b5-82ac-515b261bf2ac",
                                "text": "When we walked—I carried Linda and held Carol's hand—Carol would whisper to herself over and over, “Going to feeze to deff, going to feeze to deff.”"
                            }
                        ]
